  "description": "Bergman turns out to be funny, which means Bergman being exact about desire instead of death. Couples mismatched by age and appetite rotate through a country weekend engineered by a grandmother and a bottle of wine; by dawn the pairings have re-sorted. The light register of a director usually at his heaviest — proof the same precision plays as farce.\n\nIn Sweden at the turn of the century, members of the upper class and their servants find themselves in a romantic tangle that they try to work out amidst jealousy and heartbreak.",
